      "content": "Absolutely, happy to help! In a DC circuit, a capacitor will eventually charge up to the voltage of the power supply and then act as an open circuit; no current will flow once fully charged. Conversely, in an AC circuit, a capacitor continually charges and discharges in response to the AC voltage, allowing current to flow, but with varying amplitude. Capacitive reactance (Xc) is given by the formula Xc = 1/(2πfC), where f is the AC frequency and C is the capacitance.",
